  "raw_text": "180\n\nPana saura munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto harm/hurt someone in return, to revenge\n \n/ dañar/lastimar a alguien a cambio, para\n\nvengarse\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nUpla kum saura wan munisa taim, pana saura munaia apia sa\n \n–\n \nWhen a person harms us, we are not to harm in\n\nreturn\n \n/ Cuando una persona nos perjudica, no debemos\n \nperjudicar\n \na cambio\n)\n\nPana sin\n \n–\n \nlikewise\n \n/ igualmente\n\n(Note/Nota: can be said in reply to some greetings such as “good to see you”\n \n/ se puede decir en respuesta a algunos\n\nsaludos como \"me alegro de verte\"\n)\n\nSakuna pana, …\n \n–\n \nBut in turn, ...\n \n/ Pero a su vez, ...\n\nPanis\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npunishment, suffering\n \n/ castigo, sufrimiento\n\n(Construct:\n \nPaniska\n)\n\nPanis munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto punish, to chastise\n \n/ castigar\n\nPanis wahwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nPanis wauhwaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto suffer distress, to be agitated because of suffering\n \n/ sufrir angustia,\nestar agitado por el sufrimiento\n\nPanis wahwi lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nPanis wauhi lâka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndistress, suffering\n \n/ angustia, sufrimiento\n\nPangkaia\n \n(Alt:\n \nLî Pangkaia\n) (\ndict,dictu,my,lv,bh\n;\n \nPanhkaia\n-lfb,dictu-alt;\n \nPankaia\n-incorrect spelling /ortografía\nincorrecta) (v)\n \n–\n \nto draw water, to pick up water\n \n/ sacar agua, recoger agua\n\nPantamangka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbow\n \n/ arco\n\nPantamangka bara trisba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbow and arrow\n \n/ arco y flecha\n\nPapa\n \n(\na/t:\n \nAisa\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npapa, father\n \n/ papa\n, padre\n \n(\nS\nee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nAisa\n)\n\n(Construct:\n \nPapiki\n;\n \nPapikam\n;\n \nPapika\n)\n\nPapakni\n \n–\n \nmade for temporary use\n \n/ hecho para uso temporal\n\nUtla papakni\n \n–\n \ntemporary dwelling, temporary shelter, hut\n \n/ vivienda temporal, refugio temporal, cabaña\n\nUtla\n \nP\napakni\n \nl\niliaka\n \nba\n \n–\n \nThe\n \nFestival of Booths\n \n/\n \nLa\n \nFiesta de las Caba\nñ\nas\n\nPapaskra\n \n(\ns\nee/ver:\n \nPaskaia\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nc\nreator\n, maker, builder,\n \ncraftsman,\n \ndoer\n \n/ creador, fabricante,\n\nconstructor, artesano, hacedor\n\n(Construct:\n \nPapaskrik\ni\n;\n \nPapaskrikam\n;\n \nPapaskrika\n)\n\nBaibil Papaskra\n \n–\n \nBible’s Author, Creator of the Bible\n \n/ Autor de la Biblia, Creador de la Biblia\n\nDiara papaskra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nmaker of things, builder, craftsman\n \n/ fabricante de cosas, constructor,\nartesano\n\nPapaskra Tara\n \n–\n \nGrand Creator\n \n/ Gran creador\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nll6\n):\n \ndiara sut Papaskra tara\n \n–\n \nCreator of all things\n \n/ Creador de todas las cosas\n)\n\nSumi papaskra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \npotter\n \n/ alfarero\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nfy116\n):\n \nSumi Papaskra Tara Jehova\n \n–\n \nGreat Potter Jehovah\n \n/ Gran\n \nA\nlfarero Jehová\n)\n\nPapu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nant\n \n/ hormiga\n\nPapu naka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nant’s nest\n \n/ nido de hormigas\n\nPapulra\n \n(\ns\nee/ver:\n \nPulaia\n)\n \n(\nn\n-\nagent\n/s\n-\nagente\n,adj)\n \n–\n \nplayer, playful\n \n/ jugador, juguetón\n\nParadais\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta,lrw\n,\n \n…\n;\n \nParadaias\n-\ndict\n,\ndictu\n-\nalt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nparadise\n \n/ paraíso\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb103\n):\n \nJehova paradais ra iwma want sa\n \n–\n \nJehovah wants you to live in paradise\n \n/ Jehová quiere que vivas en el paraíso\n)\n\nParadais tasbaia\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nParadais t\nasbaya\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe paradise earth\n \n/ la tierra del paraíso\n\nParam\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nopen, manifest, plain, visible\n, clear\n \n/ abierto, manifiesto, llano, visible, claro\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh3\n):\n \nBaibil ra lika ansika param wankisa\n \n–\n \nThe Bible gives us clea\nr\n \nanswers\n \n/ La Biblia nos da respuestas claras\n)\n\nParam aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak openly, to speak clearly\n \n/ hablar abiertamente, hablar claramente\n\nParam kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\nParam marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto reveal\n \n/ revelar\n\nParam Marikan\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nReveleshen\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nRevelation\n \n(Bible book) / Apocalipsis (libro bíblico)\n\nParam pali\n \n–\n \nvery open, very clear, very manifest, very visible, very plain, openly, clearly, visibly, plainly\n \n/ muy\nabierto, muy claro, muy manifiesto, muy visible, abierto, claro, visible\n\nParam takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become clear, to become visible, to become open, to become manifest, to appear\n \n/ hacerse\nclaro, hacerse visible, abrirse, manifestarse, aparecer\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/18\n):\n \nJisas pruan wina buan piua ra param takan Pita bara disaipil\n \nî\na nani ra.\n \n–\n \nWhen Jesus was\nresurrected, he appeared to Peter and other disciples.\n \n/ Cuando Jesús resucitó, se le apareció a Pedro y a otros discípulos.)",
